# Overview
#
# Each phrase announces that the writer is about to say a thing again
# (`In other words,`), so the reader reads one point twice. The fix
# keeps the clearer of the two statements, and deletes both the other
# one and the phrase.
#
# A summary opener (`In summary,`, `In conclusion,`, `To sum up,`)
# announces that the paragraph is about to say its point again. The fix
# moves a closing summary to the start, where it tells the reader what
# the paragraph shows. The rule sits at Required, because each phrase is
# exact, and every sampled hit opened a restatement or a summary.
#
# Expression
#
# `in other words` counts only with a glued comma. `put differently`,
# `said differently`, `stated differently`, and `to put it another way`
# need the comma too. A summary opener counts with the glued comma of an
# opener.
#
# `to be clear` also needs the start of a clause after its comma. A
# clause is a subject and its verb, such as `the tests pass`. By
# default, a Weir match stops at a comma, so `let scope "Sentence"` lets
# the `to be clear` branch cross one.
#
# False Positives
#
# The bare `in other words` ends a clause (`restates it in other
# words`). Without the start of a clause after its comma, `to be clear`
# opens a list of adjectives (`comments to be clear, accurate, and
# readable`).
#
# Related Rules
#
# `That is,` stays out, because ProseLatinAbbreviation offers it as the
# fix for `i.e.`.
#
# The Recommended ProseRestatement holds `In short,`, because the opener
# also leads a point that the text has not made yet.
#
# `put simply` and `to put it simply` sit in ProseMinimizer, which
# reports every `simply` but the one before `put`, so each set of words
# draws one finding.
#
# Measurement
#
# The rule hit 77 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 20 of 20 sampled
# hits opened a restatement or a summary.
expr main [(in other words,), (simply put), (that is to say), (to be clear, [DET, PRON, PROPN, NOUN]), (in summary,), (in conclusion,), (to sum up,), (to summarize,), (all in all,), (put differently,), (said differently,), (stated differently,), (to put it another way,)]
let message "Restatement. Keep the clearer of the two statements, and delete the other one and the phrase. Move a closing summary to the start."
let description "Flags phrases that announce the writer is about to say a thing again."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
let scope "Sentence"
allows "The summary restates the claim in other words."
allows "Rewrite the comments to be clear, accurate, and readable."
